# MSG91 OTP — do not modify

OTP via MSG91 is working in production. **Do not change OTP-related code** unless the user explicitly asks for OTP/MSG91 work.

## Off-limits unless explicitly requested

- `app/msg91.py`
- OTP routes and verification in `app/routes/auth.py` (`/otp/*`, `verify_access_token`, join/forgot-password OTP handling)
- `app/static/js/msg91-registration.js`
- `app/static/js/join-registration.js`
- `app/static/js/committee-registration.js`
- `app/static/js/forgot-password-otp.js`
- `app/static/js/server-otp.js`
- OTP sections in `app/templates/landing.html`, `app/templates/pricing/register.html`, `app/templates/auth/forgot_password_otp.html`
- MSG91 env vars (`MSG91_*` in `.env`, `.env.example`, deploy/terraform secrets)
- `scripts/test-msg91*.sh`, `scripts/test-sms-otp.py`

## When building other features

- Do not refactor, “fix”, or rewire OTP as part of unrelated tasks.
- If a feature touches registration or password reset, reuse the existing widget flow; do not switch to server-side OTP or change templates/scripts listed above.
- If OTP must change to complete a task, **stop and ask the user** instead of editing these files.

## Allowed

- Read OTP files for context only.
- Change OTP code **only** when the user clearly requests OTP/MSG91 changes.
